%description:

Tcp.initialRto:rfc1122 -- the first retransmission of a SYN comes after 3 s.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "[...] 3 s is the value of RFC 1122".

The classes: the two values that the NED names, rfc6298 (1s, the default) and rfc1122 (3s;
LegacyTcp). The code: the first timeout of a SYN (TcpConnection::startSynRexmitTimer()) and
the RTO before the first measurement (TcpAlgorithmBase::initialize()). This test separates "rfc1122" from "rfc6298".

Host under test: host1; the tap drops each SYN. Observation: level 1, the second SYN of host1
comes 3 s after the first.

%# parameter: Tcp.initialRto
%# class: rfc1122
%# value: 3s
%# key: *.host1.tcp.initialRto
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpInitialRtoRfc1122")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true").drop()
                     .describe("every SYN of host1"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .describe("the first SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .never(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
              .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
              .describe("an early second SYN, 3 s after the first")
              .within(2.9))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .describe("second SYN, 3 s after the first")
             .within(0.2));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpInitialRtoRfc1122 compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.initialRto = 3s    # the parameter under test
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpInitialRtoRfc1122: PASS
